WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.810
You’re relaxing at home when there’s a
knock on the door.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:12.040
You peer through the peephole and see a small
child with their hoodie obscuring their face.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.170
You open your door and ask if they need help
but when they look up—you are staring into

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.960
black, lifeless eyes.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:24.930
It’s not hard to figure out why these creatures
horrify us so much—it’s in their name.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:30.779
Black-Eyed Children or Black-Eyed Kids, also
known as BEK, are modern monsters whose eerie

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:34.610
and unnatural appearance and behavior inspire
fear.

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:38.300
The unusual eyes are unnerving,
but it’s the age of these monsters that

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.600
really amps up the terror.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.360
What is it about “evil” children that
freaks us out so much?

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:50.739
[Monstrum intro.]

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:54.750
The first report of a Black-Eyed Kid appeared
in 1998.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:59.489
Texan reporter Brian Bethel wrote of an experience
he had two years prior while he was sitting

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:01.770
in his car near a movie theater.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:06.610
Bethel claimed that his car was approached
by two boys around the ages of 9 and 12 wearing

00:01:06.610 --> 00:01:08.590
hooded sweatshirts.

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:13.340
One appeared as an “olive-skinned, curly-headed
young man” and the other a “redheaded,

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.950
pale-skinned, freckled young man.”

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.590
Bethel opened the window a crack, and the
two boys asked for a ride to their mother’s

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:23.799
house to pick up some money so they could
see the Mortal Kombat movie.

00:01:23.799 --> 00:01:28.101
To this day, Bethel recalls that when the
second one of the boys spoke he felt an unnatural

00:01:28.101 --> 00:01:29.469
sense of dread.

00:01:29.469 --> 00:01:33.950
He pointed out the movie had already started,
and they wouldn’t make it back in time,

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:39.240
but the boys began to push harder saying things
like “They were just two kids” and that

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.959
“They didn’t have a gun or anything.”

00:01:41.959 --> 00:01:45.880
Bethel describes their voices as “mechanical”
and “rehearsed.”

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:51.090
The strange experience culminated in terror
when he realized each boy had black eyes,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.939
“soulless orbs”—with no white showing
at all.

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:59.899
Understandably unnerved, he began to drive
away, but one of the boys banged on his window

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:03.759
and angrily cried “We can’t come in unless
you tell us it’s OK.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:04.999
Let us in!”

00:02:04.999 --> 00:02:09.810
Bethel sped off, and upon checking his rearview
mirror, he noted that the strange, black-eyed

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.840
children had completely vanished.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:17.099
In 2013 Bethel wrote that his strange experience
with these children was originally shared

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:21.810
in a private communication with “a small
group of friends on an email list” that

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.490
then was leaked onto the Internet.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:29.319
I couldn’t find any evidence of this original
document, but Bethel’s story is undoubtedly

00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:32.100
the foundation of all BEK lore.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.490
And that’s how an urban legend is born.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.430
In eyewitness accounts and other stories,
the child-like creatures are frequently wearing

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:43.470
hooded clothing, although some versions claim
they are dressed in antiquated outfits.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:48.959
They have odd speech patterns, black eyes,
and perhaps most importantly—they just don’t

00:02:48.959 --> 00:02:51.810
act in a way we think children should.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.940
Similar to some vampire legends, it appears
that they must be invited into a private space.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.680
And to me this creepiness evokes fairy, demon,
and changeling vibes.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.650
Though encounters tend to end without lasting
effects, some people who’ve had run-ins

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:09.370
with these creatures report nightmares and
agoraphobia.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:14.099
Through the numerous interviews Bethel conducted
as his story circulated online, others across

00:03:14.099 --> 00:03:18.430
the world began to speak up about their own
supposed experiences with other Black-Eyed

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.430
Children.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:24.260
England in particular seems plagued by Black-Eyed
Children and they often serve as fodder for

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:27.090
tabloid magazines and newspapers.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:32.219
Like in 2014, when songwriter and paranormal
investigator Lee Brickley was interviewed

00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:36.049
by the Birmingham Mail about a sighting in
Cannock Chase, England.

00:03:36.049 --> 00:03:40.849
The sensational story was quickly picked up
by the British and international press.

00:03:40.849 --> 00:03:45.969
Brickley had been investigating rumored sightings
of a black-eyed ghost in Cannock Chase, including

00:03:45.969 --> 00:03:50.219
one where a woman and her daughter were out
for a walk when they heard screams and spotted

00:03:50.219 --> 00:03:52.290
a child wandering alone.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:55.700
The mother ran to catch up but could not find
the child.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:04:00.040
When she turned back around, a girl appearing
to be 10-years-old stood there with her hands

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.650
over her eyes.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:03.209
She asked: Are you okay?

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.700
Were you screaming?

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:09.870
The girl just dropped her hands and revealed
eyes the woman said were “completely black,

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.810
no iris, no white.”

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.040
Startled, the woman grabbed her daughter and
jumped back.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:18.180
When she looked up, expecting to see the child
- she’d vanished

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:23.620
Interestingly, Brickley also claims that this
same girl, whom he calls a “ghost,” had

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:29.430
been seen 30 years earlier in 1982 in that
same area by his own aunt, something he wrote

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:34.150
about in his 2013 book UFOs, Werewolves, &amp; The
Pig-Man.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:38.450
Brickley claims that his aunt heard a child
crying at night, and following the sobs, she

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:43.479
came upon a girl about 6-years-old who looked
up at her with completely black eyes, before

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:45.750
racing off into the woods.

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:49.160
Even a police search for the child turned
up nothing.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:53.980
The sightings of this singular female BEK
in Cannock Chase may be connected to a real-life

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:59.010
tragedy that influenced Brickley’s identification
of the creature as a ghost.

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:04.160
Cannock Chase made headlines in the 1960s
as the site of one of the largest police investigations

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:09.199
in British history—the search for the murderer
of three local schoolgirls.

00:05:09.199 --> 00:05:13.099
Some say the Black-Eyed Child of that area
is the ghost of one of the girls, and it would

00:05:13.099 --> 00:05:17.800
make sense that a young female resident who
grew up with those stories would believe she

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.300
had seen something even if it wasn’t there.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:24.300
As the urban legend of the Black-Eyed Children
evolved out of references to eyewitness accounts

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.069
of the monsters in the British and American
press, their presence across media of all

00:05:29.069 --> 00:05:31.090
kinds exploded.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:35.139
Numerous YouTube videos claim to show evidence
that such creatures exist.

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:40.610
The BEK also gained notoriety (and lore expansion)
through crowd-funded “fanfiction” texts

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:45.410
and productions like Sunshine Girl and the
Hunt for Black Eyed Kids, The Black-Eyed Children,

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.659
and Black Eyed Children: Let Me In.

00:05:47.659 --> 00:05:52.669
The comic series B.E.K. expands the monsters’s
threat with the invention of a violent origin

00:05:52.669 --> 00:05:57.970
story where regular children turn into Black-Eyed
Kids if they murder their family.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:04.500
BEK are such great modern folklore because
they defy romanticized notions of childhood

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:08.910
and the inherent goodness of children—ideas
that have evolved over time.

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:13.370
The perception of children as innocent and
weak, requiring constant adult instruction

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:17.810
both morally and physically, is a relatively
modern invention.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.949
Prior to the Romantic period, children were
largely socially insignificant.

00:06:21.949 --> 00:06:26.190
They were background characters relegated
to chores and familial duties, and little

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.190
else.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.190
Prior to the Romantic period, children were
rarely featured in Western literature, and

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:29.190
when they did they were often insignificant
background characters.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:32.440
But with the progression of the Industrial
Age in the late 18th century, as infant mortality

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:37.330
declined, and literature and philosophy regarding
child education grew alongside

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:43.330
increased scrutiny around child labor—the
cultural concept of the child changed.

00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:48.289
Childhood became a sacred cultural symbol,
a time of perceived innocence and happiness

00:06:48.289 --> 00:06:53.500
when children were not valued for their usefulness
or economic viability but rather for their

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.850
hopeful possibility and vulnerability.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:07:02.810
This continued to progress and evolve well
into the 20th century, when the seismic social

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:06.169
shifts following World War II changed everything.

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:11.490
Suddenly, youth culture and scrutiny of popular
media’s influence on children became hot

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:17.379
topics, and 1950s pop culture was flooded
with movies and literature showing “bad

00:07:17.379 --> 00:07:20.229
kids” and juvenile delinquents.

00:07:20.229 --> 00:07:24.741
Around this time, the theme of children being
born evil became a prevalent one, as we were

00:07:24.741 --> 00:07:30.380
introduced to ever younger characters with
genetically inherited threatening characteristics,

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:34.229
like a desire to kill (The Veldt; The Bad
Seed) and mind-control (Village of the Damned).

00:07:34.229 --> 00:07:38.930
Then through the 1970s and all the way into
the 90s we see a spike in horror texts with

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:43.569
children possessed by demons (The Exorcist)
or some other kind of evil entity (Pet Sematary).

00:07:43.569 --> 00:07:47.580
They’re even portrayed as the literal offspring
of Satan (Rosemary’s Baby), or the Devil

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.270
himself (The Omen).

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:50.270
The examples from this time period seem pointed?

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:54.130
The rise of the child villain can be framed
in countless ways, including an emerging fear

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:58.509
of youth culture stemming from a movement
away from traditional, conservative ideas

00:07:58.509 --> 00:08:00.530
by younger generations.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:05.479
Others argue it’s a manifestation of Freud’s
“Oedipus Complex” where it is the Id,

00:08:05.479 --> 00:08:10.840
the instinctual, unconscious part of the mind
of the child that wants to murder the parent.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.340
Or “Peter Pan Syndrome” which locates
the child’s desire to kill in an attempt

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.189
to reject their own future as an adult.

00:08:18.189 --> 00:08:23.050
And sure, as a generalized explanation for
the increase in fictional accounts of terrifying

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:24.860
children, these all make sense.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:30.229
But none of that really explains the other
key feature besides age that makes the Black-Eyed

00:08:30.229 --> 00:08:32.420
Children scary—those black eyes.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:36.710
“The eyes are the window to the soul”
is a familiar saying.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:41.970
We communicate with our eyes, and they serve
vital survival and social functions, so when

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:47.010
they appear unnaturally obscured, we become
uncomfortable—even scared.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:51.240
Scientific research does show that we tend
to track the eye movements of others as an

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.720
evolutionary social mechanism.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:58.330
Perhaps the inability to follow the gaze of
the BEK is what adds to their eeriness—and

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.960
the danger they threaten.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:03.320
They could be looking anywhere—or nowhere.

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:07.840
Unfortunately, this concept was at one point
taken to the extreme with a practice called

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:12.580
physiognomy, which is predicated on the idea
that one’s facial features and eyes could

00:09:12.580 --> 00:09:17.900
be “read” as a “natural language”
that would reveal insight about a person’s

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:22.100
character—or supposedly an indication of
their ethnic origins.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:26.530
Needless to say, there was a lot of bigotry
and racism in the practice.

00:09:26.530 --> 00:09:31.290
Although it’s roots date back to ancient
Chinese, Japanese, and Mesopotamian traditions,

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:36.260
the practice held prominent intellectual weight
in Europe until the eighteenth century.

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:40.520
Unsurprisingly, the eyes were the most important
feature to interpret.

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:43.820
According to a late 15th century text (De
homine, Galeotto Marzio 1490), eyes with no

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:47.910
whites visible were manifestations of unreliability
in a person.

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:53.140
There is also a larger cultural history of
dark eyes or black eyes being tied to inherent

00:09:53.140 --> 00:09:59.040
evilness or an inner darkness, including many
racist depictions of non-white individuals

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:02.070
in literature, including children.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:07.750
Dark or black eyes are also featured in evocations
of possession and demonic presence, and often

00:10:07.750 --> 00:10:10.060
symbolize a lack of control.

00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:15.970
To me, Black-Eyed Children are the— excuse
the pun—the offspring of four main thread:

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:20.290
One: our natural wariness of an obscured or
unusual gaze;

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.780
Two: intergenerational conflict;

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:26.440
Three: the legacy of malevolent children in
horror films;

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:31.170
and Four: the ease of which the Internet reinforces
urban legends.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:36.250
The power of the internet to expand the reach
of these creatures cannot be overstated.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:40.270
Historically, folklore and folk tradition
have been passed on through generations by

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:44.470
word of mouth and could even take years to
spread from one country or continent to the

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:50.100
other; but in modern times the world wide
web functions as a global town square, the

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:53.440
electronic equivalent of sharing stories by
the fire.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.460
I know that personally, thanks to a combination
of The Children of the Corn and the French

00:10:57.460 --> 00:11:01.300
film Them [2006], I am terrified of trick-or’-treaters.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:05.850
Which yes, makes me somewhat of a Halloween
Grinch—but it also helps me understand why

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.550
stories of BEK continue to circulate.

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:11.800
Obviously, we know that my fear of trick-or-treaters
is largely irrational.

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.110
And we know that there aren’t soulless children
out there trying to kill us.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:16.110
Right?

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:21.120
I mean, the Black-Eyed Kids are always trying
to breach the border from outside to.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:25.950
From a public space with witnesses, to a private,
more solitary one.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:29.140
Their faces are obscured, their eyes unreadable.

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:32.990
This particular urban legend seems to tap
into something deeper.

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:37.460
We are genetically programmed to care for
and protect the youngest of our species for

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.560
survival.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:42.820
So when they are portrayed as sinister and
dangerous, it is deeply unsettling.

00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:47.080
The world of BEK suggests that if you care
for children, they will kill you.

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:54.450
And if you ignore them, they will haunt you.

